1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,215
A signal is one measurement of the market,

2
00:00:02,235 --> 00:00:05,356
worked out from price and volume on finished candles.

3
00:00:05,406 --> 00:00:07,861
Each one answers a single question.

4
00:00:08,298 --> 00:00:12,801
Most signals can be read on several timeframes, from fifteen minutes to weekly.

5
00:00:12,851 --> 00:00:15,305
Hover any signal to see what it measures.

6
00:00:16,313 --> 00:00:20,474
Trend signals ask: which way is the market going, and how firmly?

7
00:00:20,524 --> 00:00:24,814
Traders use them to work with the main direction, rather than against it.

8
00:00:25,243 --> 00:00:28,615
Momentum signals ask: how fast, and how stretched?

9
00:00:28,665 --> 00:00:32,153
They help spot moves that have run hard, or are losing steam.

10
00:00:32,173 --> 00:00:36,901
A divergence is when price makes a new extreme, but momentum does not follow.

11
00:00:37,348 --> 00:00:41,296
Regime asks: what kind of market is this? Trending or ranging,

12
00:00:41,346 --> 00:00:43,679
and is volatility compressed or expanding?

13
00:00:43,699 --> 00:00:46,745
The same setup can mean different things in each.

14
00:00:47,177 --> 00:00:49,909
Structure follows the swing highs and lows:

15
00:00:49,959 --> 00:00:53,069
whether they are rising or falling, where price broke through,

16
00:00:53,089 --> 00:00:56,318
and the real price levels where swings have turned before.

17
00:00:56,761 --> 00:00:59,621
Volume asks: is the crowd behind the move?

18
00:00:59,671 --> 00:01:01,865
Rising prices on rising volume tell a

19
00:01:01,885 --> 00:01:05,176
different story from rising prices on thin volume.

20
00:01:05,610 --> 00:01:10,198
Sentiment reads recent headlines about the asset, positive or negative.

21
00:01:10,248 --> 00:01:15,177
Its history starts in November 2026 with the birth of Angstrom Signals.

22
00:01:15,611 --> 00:01:18,172
On their own, signals are ingredients.

23
00:01:18,222 --> 00:01:21,421
In Lattice you combine them into Groups, and Groups into Sets,

24
00:01:21,441 --> 00:01:24,752
so they are read together, the way a trader reads a chart.

25
00:01:25,193 --> 00:01:29,653
Every signal describes what is happening now. None of them is a prediction,

26
00:01:29,703 --> 00:01:33,288
which is why Lattice always shows a reading together with its reason.
